<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hachisuka clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hachisuka clan was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> family from Owari province that rose in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>. In 1585 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hachisuka-iemasa">Hachisuka Iemasa</a> received Awa province on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a> and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokushima">Tokushima</a> Castle, and his son Yoshishige sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> in 1600. The family ruled the Tokushima domain, with Awaji added in 1615, for the whole <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a> until the abolition of the domains in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hachisuka-clan.jpg" alt="Hachisuka clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Maru_ni_Hidari_Mannji.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
